From c5db115a21732a1df7c8dc36c1ae6d594a3c497b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jeff R. Day" <phroun@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 18:49:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] purfecterm: read-only mirror paint (one live terminal, many
 places)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add PaintMirror so a host can show ONE live terminal in several places at
once — a primary that owns the emulator, plus read-only mirrors — without the
mirrors disturbing focus, the caret, or the grid.

A mirror paint sets a per-paint mirrorPaint flag and renders the terminal as
UNFOCUSED: hollow cursor, no blink, and (above all) no platform-caret request,
so only the primary owns the cursor. paintFocused() is the effective focus for
rendering — the real focus() forced off under the flag — and is now what the
cell caret gate and gfxFocused() consult; focused() itself is unchanged, so
input routing and the emulator's own focus reporting to the child are
untouched.

A mirror also touches none of the shared buffer's write-side state, because it
draws a DIFFERENT (often smaller) rectangle than the primary:

  - updateTerminalSize early-returns under the flag, and the graphical
    fit-resize is skipped, so a mirror never resizes the child from its own
    rect (which would fight the primary and thrash the child process).
  - SetBounds under the flag still BOUNDS the mirror's row/column loop to its
    own rectangle (a mirror smaller than the grid stops at its edge instead of
    spilling rows past it) but emits no resize.
  - CheckCursorAutoScroll{,Horiz} and ClearDirty run only on the primary paint;
    from a mirror they would scroll the shared buffer to fit the mirror and the
    primary would then show the scrolled result.

No API removed; PaintMirror and paintFocused are additive. Bump Build to 13.
